5644: /*
5645:  *  @@SELFCHECK@@ -- #551.  CAN THIS FILE'S COMPARATORS STILL FAIL?  Feeds chk() and row_cmp() known answers --
5646:  *  each operand zero and past 32 bits, each of row_cmp()'s two disjuncts alone, and one pair that must NOT
5647:  *  fail -- and requires the EXACT change in `failures' for each, restoring `rows' and `failures' after every
5648:  *  probe.  Run FIRST (before any row) and LAST (after every row, before the identity row), so a comparator
5649:  *  that goes inert partway through is caught at one end or the other.  Only the success arm prints gate 2's G
5650:  *  text; the failure arm does not, and forces one failure.
5651:  *
5652:  *  WHAT IT COVERS: the rows that go through chk() and row_cmp() -- the last run prints how many calls
5653:  *  each comparator took.  Of chk()'s calls, the ones in row_ring_occupancy_sound() that pass a
5654:  *  `cond ? 1 : 0' (or `? 0 : 1') hand it a VERDICT computed at the call, not a comparison, and every
5655:  *  other row in this file compares inline: neither is covered by this block.  "Covered" means the
5656:  *  COMPARATOR is live, not that a row is.  NOT CAUGHT, DISCLOSED: a test keyed on a value, a name or a
5657:  *  position the probes do not present, in either comparator, and an edit of the code that FEEDS them
5658:  *  (row() handing row_cmp() its own want), keep every gate-2 row green -- measured, pass 2 of #551;
5659:  *  reviewed in the differential, not chased.  No line this block prints carries the self-mutant row's
5660:  *  text or "high byte" (gate 2 counts both).  Gate 2's G text is printed ONCE, by the last run, only
