1881: # A prose mention of "DEVINIT" in a comment used to reach the generated C. It cost
1882: # 358 compiler errors, no binary, gate 1 red and eleven gates skipped -- from one
1883: # comment line, which is still in the tree DELIBERATELY (rewording it would have
1884: # made the hardening deletable in silence).
1885: #
1886: # The driver runs the REAL generator in a scratch copy, so it cannot drift from
1887: # what ships, and it carries its own mutant lane. The load-bearing row is the
1888: # ORDERED NAME LIST, not a character check: measured, the half-fix that keeps
1889: # noglob but drops the anchor emits 27 extra names of which 26 are DOTLESS --
1890: # valid C identifiers that a "no bad characters" row waves straight through, and
1891: # that fail at link time instead of parse time.
1892: AGLOG=$LOGDIR/diff_autodev_gen.log
